('127.888.d.29.A',4,'The swashplate transfers control inputs to the:','["landing skids", "fuel tank", "tail boom", "rotating rotor blades"]'::jsonb,3,'Swashplate.','original'),
('127.888.d.29.B',3,'A mechanic opens the maintenance manual to the track and balance section for the main rotor. She is:','["identifying and locating helicopter rotor blade track and balance procedures", "painting blades", "guessing", "ignoring blades"]'::jsonb,0,'Track and balance data.','original'),
('127.888.d.29.B',4,'Blade track and balance procedures are found in the:','["paint guide", "aircraft maintenance manual", "seat manual", "owner''s flyer"]'::jsonb,1,'Where to look.','original'),
('127.888.d.29.C',3,'A mechanic opens the manual to the steps and tools for rigging the cyclic and collective. She is:','["ignoring rigging", "guessing", "identifying and locating procedures needed to rig helicopter controls", "painting controls"]'::jsonb,2,'Rigging data.','original'),
('127.888.d.29.C',4,'Rigging a helicopter''s controls often requires special:','["seat covers", "paint", "stickers", "rigging pins or fixtures"]'::jsonb,3,'Rig tools.','original'),
('127.888.d.29.D',3,'A mechanic opens the manual to the steps for tracking and balancing the rotor with a strobe and a balancer. She is:','["identifying and locating procedures to track and balance a rotor system", "ignoring the rotor", "painting the rotor", "guessing"]'::jsonb,0,'Rotor T&B.','original'),
('127.888.d.29.D',4,'A blade tracking check measures:','["cabin heat", "whether blade tips follow the same path", "fuel flow", "tire pressure"]'::jsonb,1,'Tracking.','original'),
('127.888.d.30.A',3,'A student labels the potable water tank, pump, filter and faucets and explains how water moves through them. She is:','["describing seats", "avoiding water", "identifying the components and explaining the basic operation of potable water systems", "describing tires"]'::jsonb,2,'Potable water.','original'),
('127.888.d.30.A',4,'A potable water system supplies water that is:','["hydraulic fluid", "waste", "fuel", "safe for drinking and washing"]'::jsonb,3,'Potable.','original'),
('127.888.d.30.B',3,'A student labels the lavatory toilet, waste tank and rinse system and explains how waste is stored. She is:','["identifying the components and explaining the basic operation of lavatory waste systems", "describing seats", "avoiding waste", "describing tires"]'::jsonb,0,'Waste system.','original'),
('127.888.d.30.B',4,'Waste from a lavatory is stored in a:','["water tank", "waste tank until it is serviced on the ground", "hydraulic tank", "fuel tank"]'::jsonb,1,'Waste tank.','original'),
('127.888.d.30.C',3,'A ground crew learns how often to drain, flush and refill the water and waste tanks. She is:','["ignoring service", "describing tires", "describing servicing requirements for water and waste systems", "describing seats"]'::jsonb,2,'Servicing needs.','original'),
